# Secrets — never commit. .env.example and .env.j2 are tracked on purpose:
# IaC-Stack's env-file.yml treats a missing template as success and the service
# would start with every ${VAR} interpolated empty (same rule as rss-reader).
#
# The secret files are named one by one rather than caught by `.env.*` plus a
# `!` negation, because this file has a second reader: IaC-Stack's rsync-build
# translates every line into an `--exclude`, and a leading `!` there does not
# un-exclude one pattern — it clears every rule collected above it. The role
# refuses the whole deploy rather than mistranslate it.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Local cache / state
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
cache/
data/

# Build output
/git-planner
/dist/
/bin/

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# Editor / OS
# The impeccable design hook keeps its config here (committed — the two
# rule suppressions are reviewable decisions that belong to this repo) next to
# a per-run cache and a pending-findings file, which do not.
.impeccable/hook.cache.json
.impeccable/hook.pending.json
.DS_Store
.idea/
# Whole directory, for the same reason as above — nothing in it is tracked.
.vscode/

# Go
*.test
*.out
vendor/
